# Upstream CLC corpora are vendored byte-exact and verified by SHA-256.
# Any end-of-line conversion would change the bytes and break the pins, so
# these files must never be normalized. Without this rule, core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites them to CRLF on Windows checkouts while Linux CI stays LF.
rust/clc-rust-cleanroom/vectors/clc-v1/*.json -text
rust/clc-rust-cleanroom/vectors/clc-d/*.json -text

# The CLC-A core corpora sit at the vectors/ root rather than in a subdirectory,
# so they need their own rule. They are upstream files too: their committed
# blobs hash to 3c1a5672… (vectors.json) and f00ed1f4… (property-cases.json),
# which are the exact digests the CLC registry baseline quotes. Normalization
# would make a Windows checkout hash differently from the registry entry.
rust/clc-rust-cleanroom/vectors/clc-a-core-vectors.json -text
rust/clc-rust-cleanroom/vectors/property-cases.json -text
